<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton output reaches 2.26 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton output reaches 2.26 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output reached 2.26 million 375-lb bales by October 25 compared to 1.487 million in the year-ago period, the state-run Cotton Export Corp of Pakistan said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said in its weekly figures that ginners had sold 1.59 million bales to textile mills compared to 1.11 million in the year-ago period, while 0.66 million bales remained unsold.</p>
<p>Revised official estimates put the crop between 9.2 and 9.5 million, down from a target of 10 million bales. In 1995/96, Pakistan produced 9.94 million bales of cotton.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-568519</p>
</text>
